{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794492472,"nonce":"SE/NgeD2bzHAymwHT4qOUsV6t6g=","title":"An image inside a moving card is drawn under the card's own background","message":"Seen in the node table repro window (the 'Image (falls back)' tile, FALLBACKS=1): a card with a background and an image child, under .motion().translate_x(..), shows no image at all while it moves. A card with the same children and no motion shows the image (checked in the harness: the pixel at the image is the image's, green).\n\nIn the harness (scene 'motion, an image' in crates/blinc_recorder/tests/animation_paths.rs) the vector reference, which every path is held to, has no image either, so this is the full paint and not the table: the image sits at the card's rest position under the card, and only a sliver shows past the card's edge once it has moved. Motion text and SVG are drawn after the dynamic batch they belong to (dispatch_motion_subtree_overlay_pools); images are not, so they are drawn before the dynamic batch and the card's background covers them.\n\nFix direction: draw the images of a motion subtree after its dynamic geometry, as text and SVG are, and place them by the binding's change since the paint on the CPU (NodeRow::apply_to_rect and the rotation in css_affine are the twins of what a row does). That also takes images and SVGs off the full-repaint fallback in 122c606: today an image or SVG inside a bound node makes every frame a full paint while it moves.\n\nRelated: 122c606, e238df7.","files":null}]}